# Intentionally empty — do NOT delete this file.
#
# Husky's shim (.husky/_/h) bails with `[ ! -f "$s" ] && exit 0` before it sources
# ~/.config/husky/init.sh. That init script is what dispatches to the machine-wide
# ~/.git-hooks/<hook>, so removing this file as "dead code" silently disables every
# global pre-push guard for this repository.
#
# The repo itself has no pre-push work of its own: CI gates the suite, and
# lint-staged already ran at commit time.
#
# No shebang, here or in the sibling hooks: a husky v9 hook file is a plain command
# list, sourced by the generated shim in .husky/_/ which carries the
# `#!/usr/bin/env sh` itself. A shebang in a user hook file is the deprecated v8 form.
